  "worked_solution": "We know that Susan has $\\frac{17}{9}$ of a pound of walnuts.\n\nTo calculate the amount that she ate, we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{3}$ by $\\frac{17}{9}.$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times \\frac{17}{9}=\\frac{1\\times 17}{3\\times 9}=\\frac{17}{27}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Susan ate $\\frac{17}{27}$ of  a pound of walnuts.",
